# Search-scope control for ripgrep and other tools that honor .ignore.
#
# Two separate problems are solved here.
#
# 1. The parent SARP repository's .ignore lists "BasicRenderer/" so that searches
#    of SARP's own code are not swamped by this submodule. ripgrep applies parent
#    ignore files during traversal, and that pattern also matches THIS repository's
#    own source directory (BasicRenderer/BasicRenderer/). Without the negation
#    below, `rg` run from here returns thousands of vendored files and not one line
#    of BasicRenderer's own code.
!BasicRenderer/

# 2. The vendored submodules below are ~6,400 of the ~6,800 files ripgrep would
#    otherwise walk. They have their own histories and are not edited here.
#
#    To search one deliberately, opt in explicitly:
#      rg --no-ignore <pattern> GPU-Reshape/
GPU-Reshape/
FidelityFX-SDK/
xatlas/
PyNifly/
geometry-central/
openpbr-bsdf/
tree-sitter-hlsl/
volk/

# BasicRHI/, OpenRenderGraph/, BasicTelemetry/ and ORGModuleServices/ are NOT
# listed. They are separate submodules but first-party components of this project
# -- the README describes the BasicRHI / OpenRenderGraph / BasicRenderer split as
# intentional -- and code here calls into them constantly, so they stay searchable.
